RCA_generator: source attribution and license scope

Original code and scientific contribution

RCA_generator is adapted from the vessel_tree_generator code accompanying:

A multi-stage neural network approach for coronary 3D reconstruction from uncalibrated X-ray angiography images
Kritika Iyer, Brahmajee K. Nallamothu, C. Alberto Figueroa, and
Raj R. Nadakuditi. Scientific Reports 13, 17603 (2023).
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-44633-2
Original code: https://github.com/kritiyer/vessel_tree_generator

The upstream vessel-generation implementation forms the foundation of this
package. Its contributions include centerline augmentation, tube construction,
forward projection, and the supplied RCA control-point assets. We explicitly
acknowledge the original authors and contributors for this code and these
assets. Please cite the source paper when using the adapted generator.

License for inherited code and assets

The original upstream license notice is retained verbatim:

This code is meant for academic research purposes only (non-commercial use).

Source: https://github.com/kritiyer/vessel_tree_generator/blob/main/license.md

These terms continue to apply to inherited code and control-point assets.
The MIT license below does not replace the upstream terms or relicense those
materials. See license.md and NOTICE.md for the upstream notice and further
source references.

License for authorized project-owned contributions

Xi Chen, et al. contribute adaptations and additions for the single-RCA
generation and paired-projection workflow. Only contributions for which they
hold the necessary rights are covered by the following MIT license.

